+# Operational readiness: npm run verify runs the rituals suite and prints the ledger check summary (informational)
+
+```
+change: package.json adds test:rituals and ledger:info (node tools/ledger.mjs check --summary, always exit 0) and runs both in verify before check; check is unchanged
+change-tier: 2
+paths: package.json, tests/dispatch/verify-scripts.test.mjs, company/engineering/readiness/2026-10-17-assessment-verify-scripts.md
+author: tools-lead
+board: none yet (chief of staff to file; source: company/reviews/org/2026-10-17-external-assessment.md §3 and Appendix B "Budgeting")
+risks: none added or closed
+links: company/engineering/readiness/2026-10-17-assessment-tooling-fixes.md (the tier-1 tool changes this wires up); company/ops/token-budget.md section 6
+```
+
+Status: **awaiting principal-engineer-ops**. Tier 2 because `package.json` is tier 2 in company/engineering/readiness/paths.json ("scripts and dependencies"). The author does not approve it. It is held in its own commit, so the tier-1 commit can merge without it.
+
+## 1. What can fail
+- **The new step fails verify.** It cannot: `--summary` exits 0 in every case, including 45 ledger errors (tests/dispatch/hard-budget.test.mjs asserts this). The only way it fails is if `tools/ledger.mjs` throws while it imports the register, for example on an unreadable projects.json. The full check fails in that case too.
+- **People read "verify passed" as "the budget is fine".** The line says "informational, never fails verify" and gives the error count, which was 45 on 2026-10-17 (history 33, behavioral-econ 11, lifehacks-engine-v2 1, matching the assessment). `npm run check` (protected CI) still does not include the ledger. Wiring it there needs an amendment to tools/company.mjs.
+- **test:rituals fails.** It reads the real records through git. CI has git, and a checkout without git history only loses records, which the test tolerates.
+
+## 2. How we would know
+The verify log prints the line. CI does not run verify (assessment finding 5), so this is local only.
+
+## 3. How to roll back
+`git revert <sha>`. No data.
+
+## 4. Capacity
+About 0.5 s added to verify, and no build.
+
+## 5. Security / 6. Data
+None.
+
+## 7. Risks
+None.
